Removing a Directory (rm -R mydirectory)
If you try to remove a directory using plain rm mydirectory, Linux blocks the operation with an error:

Plaintext
rm: cannot remove 'mydirectory': Is a directory
Linux does this deliberately to prevent accidental data destruction. To delete a directory and everything inside it, you must use the -R (or lowercase -r) flag, which stands for recursive.

Bash
rm -R mydirectory
